# Write in your own editor

If you prefer to write in another app, link a folder on your computer to your book. Each text file in the folder becomes a chapter, and one click brings your changes in. This needs Chrome or Edge.

1. Put your chapters in one folder, one text file each, such as `chapter01.txt`. Files ending in `.txt` or `.md` are used.
2. In SEED.html, click the [Book]{.ui} tab, then [Contents]{.ui}.
3. Click [Link a folder]{.ui} and choose the folder.
4. A window lists what will change: new chapters, and chapters whose text is different. Click [Apply]{.ui}.

After you edit the files, click [Sync folder]{.ui} in the same place to bring the changes in. You always see the list first, and nothing changes until you apply it.

New files join the end of the chapter list. A sync never changes the order of your chapters, and never removes a chapter unless you choose to.

The link belongs to this browser on this computer. It is not part of the book.
